    "media:imagetext": "727-200\nI PIEDMONT\nIMPORTANT INFORMATION to Our Passengers\nYou are flying aboard a Boeing 727-200. It is unlikely we will encounter\na situation requiring emergency preparations, but it is good practice\nto be acquainted with the safety features we have provided for you on\nthis aircraft.\n•EMERGENCY EXITS\nWINDOW EXITS\nForward\nEntry\nDoor\nService\nDoor\nI. To release\nwindow - grasp\nhandle anc\npull down.\nWindow\nExits\nWindow\nExits\n2. To remove\nwindow -\npull inward\nand lift up\nas shown.\nRear\nService\nDoor\nRear\nService\nDoor\nRear Entry\nFORWARD PASSENGER AND SERVICE DOOR\n1. Turn handle\ndirection of\narrow.\n2. As hinged\nside moves\nin push other\nside out.\n3. Pull handle\nto inflate\nslide.\n4.\nJump and\nsit in slide.\nOPE\nREAR ENTRY DOOR\nThis Door Cannot Be Opened\nIn Flight\nTurn handle to\nopen.\nPull inward\non door.\nStair Controi\nPush Handle\nstair will fall.\n0943-00110 (Original 8-1-81)",
