    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "727-200\nI PIEDMONT\nIMPORTANT INFORMATION to Our Passengers\nYou are flying aboard a Boeing 727-200. It is unlikely we will encounter\na situation requiring emergency preparations, but it is good practice\nto be acquainted with the safety features we have provided for you on\nthis aircraft.\n•EMERGENCY EXITS\nWINDOW EXITS\nForward\nEntry\nDoor\nService\nDoor\nI. To release\nwindow - grasp\nhandle anc\npull down.\nWindow\nExits\nWindow\nExits\n2. To remove\nwindow -\npull inward\nand lift up\nas shown.\nRear\nService\nDoor\nRear\nService\nDoor\nRear Entry\nFORWARD PASSENGER AND SERVICE DOOR\n1. Turn handle\ndirection of\narrow.\n2. As hinged\nside moves\nin push other\nside out.\n3. Pull handle\nto inflate\nslide.\n4.\nJump and\nsit in slide.\nOPE\nREAR ENTRY DOOR\nThis Door Cannot Be Opened\nIn Flight\nTurn handle to\nopen.\nPull inward\non door.\nStair Controi\nPush Handle\nstair will fall.\n0943-00110 (Original 8-1-81)",
      "- PIEDMONT\nAUTOMATIC\nOXYGEN\nSYSTEM\nThe higher altitudes at which this aircraft operates require prompt\nuse of the automatic oxygen system in case of any sudden change\nin cabin pressure. Should a decompression occur, oxygen masks\nwill drop down automatically. Take nearest mask and promptly place\nover nose and mouth and lean back in your seat.\nBRACE\nPOSITIONS\nIn an emergency\nsituation your\nFlight Attendant\nmay request you\nto assume one of\nthe Bracing\nPositions shown.\nINSTRUCTIONS FOR USE OF SEAT BELTS\nLIFT TO UNFASTEN\nHold buckle and pull top strap for a tight fit. Please keep your seat\nbelt fastened at all times while in your seat.\nFLOTATION\nCUSHIONS\n1. Lift up at rear\nof cushion\n2. Push down on\nfront to unhook\nfor holding\nThe cushion you are seated on will float. In water landing remove\nyour cushion\nas shown in diagram and take it with you in leaving\nthe aircraft.\nPORTABLE ELECTRONIC DEVICES\nFederal Aviation Agency (FAA) regulation prohibits the operation in-\nflight of certain portable electronic devices since they can interfere\nwith the aircraft's navigation system. Please check with the Flight\nAttendant before operating your radio, dictating machine or recorder.\nPlease Do Not Remove This Card From Aircraft\n0943-00110 (Original 8-1-81)\n2002.127.486"
    ],
